  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are NNN different colours of balloons, numbered 111 to NNN. The iii-th colour balloon costs exactly iii rupees. That is, a balloon of colour 111 costs 111 rupee, balloon of colour 222 costs 222 rupees and so on.\n\nYou bought AiA_iAi​ balloons of the iii-th colour, what is the total cost of all the balloons you bought?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN - the number of colours.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the total cost of the balloons.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\le N \\le 1001≤N≤100",
      "1≤Ai≤1001 \\le A_i \\le 1001≤Ai​≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n1\n5\n3\n1 1 1",
        "output": "5\n6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : You have 555 balloons of colour 111, so a total cost of 5⋅15 \\cdot 15⋅1.\nTest Case 2 : 111 balloon each of colours 111, 222, and 333, thus a cost of 1+2+3=61 + 2 + 3 = 61+2+3=6."
      }
    ]
  },
